From 071d350c22b3e182bc2f0d58d6994845e88656e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:46:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Krylov solvers of hypre: absolute tolerance

The parameter `AbsoluteTolerance` was read by the generators of
`HypreGMRES` and `HypreFGMRES` but refused by their lists of allowed
parameters, and `HypreFGMRES` gave it to `SetTol` (relative tolerance),
`mfem::HypreFGMRES` having no `SetAbsTol` method. It is now accepted by
the three Krylov solvers of hypre (`HyprePCG` included) and given to
hypre (`HYPRE_ParCSRFlexGMRESSetAbsoluteTol` for FGMRES).

New test HypreKrylovAbsoluteToleranceTest: with an absolute tolerance
much larger than the initial residual, each solver stops at once.
---
 src/LinearSolverFactory.cxx                | 14 ++-
 tests/CMakeLists.txt                       |  3 +
 tests/HypreKrylovAbsoluteToleranceTest.cxx | 99 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/HypreKrylovAbsoluteToleranceTest.cxx

